<title>ESTONIA: CONSTRUCTION GROWTH SLOWS IN Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>CONSTRUCTION GROWTH SLOWS IN Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's construction industry reached 1.04 billion kroons in the first quarter of 1997, a one percent increase from the same period in 1996, the country's statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>During the first quarter in 1996, construction activities rose six percent, it added in a statement.  </p>
<p>Most construction activities or 96 percent were in Estonia.</p>
<p>Approximately 32,000 employees were working in the construction sector in the first quarter of the year.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
